AudioScope 0.2.0 — modified version, 2026-10-05.
Package dev.audioscope; independent name, icon and interface.

This software is a fork / edited derivative of ShizuCallRecorder and CallVault.
https://github.com/kitsumed/ShizuCallRecorder
https://github.com/madkongo/CallVault

Playback AudioPolicy reflection, on-device ADB identity persistence and
detached Binder delivery, local-device mDNS discovery, notification reply pairing
and Wireless debugging intent navigation were adapted from CallVault, upstream source commit
8ef410766e05f5b0eec3d83da4cbd3faf29728de, copyright The CallVault Authors.
Original attribution and the upstream Section 7 terms are retained in LICENSE
and displayed in the application Settings/About section.

AudioScope modifications: Material 3 UI, selectable accents, manual capture
catalog, live monitoring and waveform rows, recording controls, timestamped PCM
pipes, signal health, per-source formats, WAV/routing/Matroska exports and labs.
Version 0.2 adds editable source layouts, density views, actionable notifications,
a waveform scrubber and media-session player, public MediaStore exports,
app-wide format propagation, debounced call automation and helper cleanup.

Dependencies are not relicensed by this notice: Material Components and Shizuku
(Apache 2.0), libadb-android (GPL-3.0-or-later OR Apache 2.0; chosen Apache 2.0), Conscrypt (Apache 2.0), Bouncy Castle
(MIT-style license). Their respective upstream notices and binary metadata apply.

GPL-3.0-or-later, with upstream additional terms in LICENSE. No warranty.

Version 0.3 adds explicit phone/Bluetooth routing, manual headset previews,
SAF folder exports and metadata, multiple signal recommendations, full-screen
recording detail, indicator/motion fixes and optional call-aware file naming.
The storage and naming designs were compared with CallVault SafHelper,
RecordingFileNameFormatter and VoipCallerName; the new Java implementations
are independently written. Upstream capture/license attribution remains above.
